        "content": "<p>jrandolf opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14800\">PR #14800</a> from <code>jrandolf:wasi-0.3.2</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This updates the vendored WASIp3 WITs to the 0.3.2 release of WASI, so <code>wasmtime-wasi</code> and <code>wasmtime-wasi-http</code> now implement the 0.3.2 versions of the interfaces. Apart from version numbers the WITs are the same as 0.3.0; the only other difference is a doc comment about casing in <code>wasi:http</code>'s <code>fields</code>.</p>\n<p>Components built against 0.3.0, which includes everything Rust's <code>wasm32-wasip3</code> target produces today, keep working because imports and exports are matched on semver-compatible versions. I've added a CLI test that runs the existing p3 WAT test at <code>@0.3.0</code> against the new host to make sure that stays true.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 632905292,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792391344
