    },
    {
        "content": "<p>alexcrichton <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14800#issuecomment-6270173557\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14800\">PR #14800</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'll note that given how WASI versioning works we cannot land this yet. WASI 0.3.1 requires <code>map&lt;K, V&gt;</code> and the <code>(implements ...)</code> features to be supported, and neither is <a href=\"https://docs.wasmtime.dev/stability-wasm-proposals.html#component-model-proposals\">on-by-default right now</a>. Notably <code>implements</code> has no fuzzing and <code>map</code> has been fuzzed for a bit and might be ready. I see sibling PRs for these, however.</p>\n</blockquote>",
